# Deliberately IDENTICAL to firmware/board_check/sdkconfig.defaults, which is
# the only configuration OBSERVED to boot on this board (2026-08-23, and again
# cold 2026-08-24 with the SD card inserted).
#
# The vendor's 09_sdmmc/sdkconfig.defaults additionally sets
# CONFIG_FREERTOS_HZ=1000, CONFIG_ESP_DEFAULT_CPU_FREQ_MHZ_240=y and
# CONFIG_ESP32S3_DATA_CACHE_LINE_64B=y. With those three, this app hung during
# app startup between "Disabling RNG early entropy source" and the octal_psram
# banner -- i.e. in PSRAM init -- and hung hard enough to wedge the USB-Serial-
# JTAG peripheral, so esptool could no longer reach download mode without the
# BOOT button. The cache-line setting is the prime suspect because it is the one
# that interacts with the PSRAM cache, but this has NOT been bisected: all three
# were removed together. Do not re-add them casually; if you want them, add one
# at a time and be ready to hold BOOT.
CONFIG_IDF_TARGET="esp32s3"
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHMODE_QIO=y
CONFIG_ESPTOOLPY_FLASHSIZE_16MB=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_MODE_OCT=y
CONFIG_SPIRAM_SPEED_80M=y
